Z||000000||loafer87gt||03-11-2000||02:06 PM||||Wahoo! I have finally found the culprit for the power loss I was experiencing. While waxing my car yesterday I decided to check the K&N air filter, sure enough it was covered with about 1/4 of oily muck. I used my cleaneer and oiled it again and took it out for a drive, and whew, BIG difference. I don't know why it got so dirty so quick (I cleaned about 5 months ago). Anyways, to top off my night, some jaybronee in a new V6 Firebird punched it an intersection ahead of me and I followed him. He hit the brakes and pulled into the other lane. At the next set of lights, all I saw was silk shirts and goldchains in the Fierbird so I thought I was going to get carjacked. To my surprise, the when the light turned green he took off with a flurry of rubber. I was totally caught off guard, I launched normally at 1000 RPMs, but in about 1/2 block I was almost caught up to him. at the next intersection he made a right turn and ran away. This is great, I was really getting worried when my car was running bad, I would even cringe when a Civic pulled up next to me, for fear that he would want to race. Not anymore! Anyways, I'm going out to flaunt my newly found balls on the main drag in my freshly waxed GT. Long live the Fiero.||||reg||1
